#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run on quantum hardware with IBM Quantum Compute Service {#run-on-quantum-"
"hardware-with-ibm-quantum-compute-service}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IBM Quantum&reg; Compute Service, formerly called the Qiskit Runtime "
"Service, is the cloud-based service for executing quantum computations on "
"IBM Quantum hardware. The `qiskit-ibm-runtime` package is a client for that "
"service, and is the successor to the Qiskit IBM Provider.  Quantum Compute "
"streamlines quantum computations and provides optimal implementations of the"
" Qiskit primitive base classes for IBM Quantum hardware. To get started with"
" IBM Quantum primitives, visit the [documentation](/guides/primitives).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum Compute is designed to use additional classical and quantum compute "
"resources, including techniques such as error suppression and error "
"mitigation, to return a higher-quality result from executing quantum "
"circuits on quantum processors. Examples include dynamical decoupling for "
"error suppression, and readout mitigation and zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE)"
" for error mitigation. Learn how to configure these options on the "
"[Configure error mitigation](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-"
"techniques) page.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum Compute also includes three types of execution modes for running "
"your quantum program on IBM&reg; hardware: [Job, Session, and "
"Batch](/guides/execution-modes), each of which have different use cases and "
"implications for the quantum job queue. A Job is a single query to a "
"primitive that can be run over a specified number of shots. Sessions allow "
"you to efficiently run multiple jobs in iterative workloads on quantum "
"computers. Batch mode allows you to submit all your jobs at once for "
"parallel processing. Note that Open Plan users cannot submit session jobs.\n"
msgstr ""

