#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Is Quantum Compute open-source? {#is-quantum-compute-open-source}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The short answer is, _not all of it_. The software that handles the "
"technicalities of running your quantum program on an IBM Quantum device "
"(including any error mitigation and suppression) is **not** open-source. "
"However, the client software library `qiskit-ibm-runtime` (which is the "
"interface for users to access IBM Quantum Compute Service), the Qiskit SDK "
"running on the server side, and some of the software used for error "
"mitigation, **are** open-source.  To get involved with Qiskit open-source "
"efforts, visit our GitHub organization at "
"[github.com/Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit) and [github.com/Qiskit-"
"Extensions](https://github.com/Qiskit-Extensions/).\n"
msgstr ""
